yippee-ki-yay movie lovers it's Jan here  if you've ever had a pet you've probably  wondered what it's thinking or what it  gets up to when you're not there and  that's essentially the premise of the  secret life of pets  basically it's Toy Story for our  four-legged furry or feathered friends  the movie features lots of cool  characters who are interestingly  designed and smartly voiced by a cast of  well-known actors including comedian  Louie CK and modern families Eric  Stonestreet who lend their vocal chords  to the movies to Maine Purchase Max and  Duke I also loved Lake Bell as the fat  cat Chloe and Jenny slate who did the  voice of bellwether and Zootopia is  wonderful as a super fluffy but badass  Pomeranian called Gidget who adores  telenovelas Kevin Hart is also just  flat-out fantastic as incredibly fluffy  and equally insane bunny snowball and  Albert Brooks who you loved heard as  Marlon in finding Nero and finding dory  is reliably on form as the hungry hawk  Tiberius screenwriters Ken Dario and  Cinco Paul who did the despicable Me  movies and Brian Lynch who did minions  give us a script that keeps at the pace  to route moving forward with plenty of  action and lots of laughs including  visual comedy animal behavior based gags  and some amusing nods to other movies  speaking of which look out for my video  on this movie's Easter eggs and  references lewiston superb set pieces  and montages right from the start where  were introduced to the movie's main pets  there's also a clever scene which shows  the ingenious ways that pets get around  the city and a crazy funny fantasy  sequence directors Chris Renault and  yarrow Cheney do a good job keeping us  entertained during the movies 90 minute  runtime though the film doesn't quite  have the depth heart or emotion of  Pixar's best movies and its story beats  do feel pretty familiar animation wise  the movies really bright and colorful  and gives us a rather beautiful version  of New York in fact there's a gorgeous  shot that flies through New York City at  the start giving us all the typical  sights you know the Statue of Liberty  Brooklyn Bridge the yellow cabs the  Empire State Central Park and so on but  it's all gorgeously lit basically if you  enjoyed the Despicable Me and minions  movies and odds-on you'll enjoy this too  and I can definitely see them making  more of these The Secret Life of pets  movies in future Owen  before the secret life of pets starts  begin a short film called MOA minions  featuring everyone's favorite banana  loving mischief-makers who proved to be  as much fun as ever and it's nice to see  them again ahead of next summer's  Despicable Me 3 so to sum up the secret  life of pets is a colorfully animated  vibrant and energetically paced feature  which pulls back the curtain on what our  pets get up to when left alone in terms  of story and emotion it doesn't quite  reach the level of the thematically  similar Toy Story or fellow animal  features Zootopia however it is a  charming flick with some fab characters  and voice cast and a bundle of laughs  and we get an added minions shorts so  what's not to like the secret life of  pets gets three and a half out of 5  flicks now what did you think of the  secret life of pets and the minions  short and what would you like to see in  Despicable Me 3 let me know in the  comments below  if you liked this review I'd love it if  you'd share it and do subscribe for more  movie reviews Easter egg videos and  amazing movie facts click the links here  to check those out thanks for watching  and see you next time you'll be going  movie lovers
 

